{"title":"2000 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 22","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Power_Solve\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Power Solve</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The graph below shows a portion of the curve defined by the quartic polynomial <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/4/4c4150b948b7f0e5195845c66cdb4d5b1eda7cc6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x) = x^4 + ax^3 + bx^2 + cx + d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"250\" height=\"19\" />. Which of the following is the smallest?\n</p><p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:2000_12_AMC-22.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/5/5e/2000_12_AMC-22.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"419\" height=\"322\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/3/c5397555112fec6c2d35d394240f13c186714453.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ P(-1)\\\\ \\textbf{(B)}\\ \\text{The\\ product\\ of\\ the\\ zeros\\ of\\ } P\\\\ \\textbf{(C)}\\ \\text{The\\ product\\ of\\ the\\ non-real\\ zeros\\ of\\ } P \\\\ \\textbf{(D)}\\ \\text{The\\ sum\\ of\\ the\\ coefficients\\ of\\ } P \\\\ \\textbf{(E)}\\ \\text{The\\ sum\\ of\\ the\\ real\\ zeros\\ of\\ } P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"317\" height=\"97\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> has degree <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, it may have at most <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/d/78d52a85b257a993d399067b367c087271f27d97.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4-1=3$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"73\" height=\"13\" /> turning points.  Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> has no turning points (and thus no real roots) which are not seen.\n</p><p>Approximate the value of each answer choice using the graph.\n</p><p>Choice (A): According to the graph, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/0/fb0296032bb63072d0befb73fc545866bbdac0c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(-1) \\approx 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"87\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>Choice (B): By Vieta's rules, the product of the roots of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/5/4650e9acc1815903b8edd4e0f429f9d2ac8a947a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d = P(0) \\approx 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"106\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>Choice (C): The product of the real roots of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is approximately <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/8/2a8f3239699b512eef82865e5f948afe7b7a2329.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1.5 \\cdot 3.5 = 5.25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"118\" height=\"14\" />, so the product of the non-real roots is approximately <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/c/17cf95018adc92a2d225d1643a024bd6a32ec1be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{5}{5.25} &lt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"71\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>Choice (D): The sum of the coefficients of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/4/c346b6d7546cd8cf89ef0437890eb0928c537b49.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(1) \\approx 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"73\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>Choice (E): The sum of the real roots of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/8/d180341fed714770e4c7b3d2cd44cf78f6565745.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1.5 + 3.5 = 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"104\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>Therefore, the smallest of these is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/4/4840288cdea2947a1f0166f1f3b2c6bb32221317.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}\\ \\text{The\\ product\\ of\\ the\\ non-real\\ zeros\\ of\\ } P}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"331\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>Edit: In  Choice (D) you have to subtract 1 because of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/0/2f0078b54474db2dbf6219e8386b9b62c4405c94.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^4$\" width=\"17\" height=\"15\" /> at the start.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Power_Solve\">Video Solution by Power Solve</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Power Solve\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=mjEPBv4hxvI\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=mjEPBv4hxvI</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/MMIEbkGu-k8\">https://youtu.be/MMIEbkGu-k8</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12\" title=\"2000 AMC 12\">2000 AMC 12</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems\" title=\"2000 AMC 12 Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Answer_Key\" title=\"2000 AMC 12 Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2000 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 21\">Problem 21</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2000 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 23\">Problem 23</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2000 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2000 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2000 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2000 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.p